    "q-340103": {
      "dom_id": "step-q340103",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given the function  $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2\\cdot {3}^{x}-1$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2\\cdot {3}^{x}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}+2\\cdot {3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{1}{x}+2\\cdot {3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3))|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}+2\\cdot {3}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\  & =1+6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
